nths  is going to be  if it's a genuine engagement and we have  to be out there and listening but if  we're just  doing you've been doing that for 18  months you haven't just suddenly  kissed time hasn't just suddenly come  into power some people would say that  what i'm asking you for i'm giving you a  platform  to speak to our viewers to speak to  people of the uk about what the big  vision is and you've actually ducked it  isn't that exactly the issue let's take  work  let's take work let's take work as one  uh  as one as one issue we know that one of  the problems  is that there have not been enough good  new secure jobs  in every single part of the country so  that every  place every town every city every county  can be the best place to grow up the  best place to grow old and the best  place to live and to work that  investment hasn't  been coming in so we've seen the good  old manufacturing jobs replaced by  low paid insecure jobs in the gig  economy and that isn't what people need  to see  now we have to work out how we are going  to work with the different regions to  bring in the investment  to sustain the good jobs of the future  that can give everybody the security  they need that their work that they can  get a job in their locality that is  going to see them and their families  through the future now one of the key  ways of doing that is through devolution  it's through opening up power so all the  decisions aren't taken  uh in in in whitehall but many more  decisions taken  in localities uh by people who  understand how their localities work  better  now the government has been trailing for  the last two years  a devolution bill that was set up their  proposals for that  we got the queen's speech just um just  last week  no sign of the devolution bill they  dropped it and the reason i think  they've dropped it  is because labour won 11 of the 13 metro  mayoral  elections the conservatives are  frightened that when people see labour  in power they like